    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0457" n="1191" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1191"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Muruaga to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of Spain, has
                    the honor to bring to the knowledge of the honorable Secretary of State that,
                    according to an official communication from the consul of his nation, volunteers
                    for the island of Cuba are being publicly recruited at New Orleans, at the
                    enlistment pay of $35 monthly and with the manifest purpose of hostilities
                    against a friendly power.</p>
                <p>The undersigned takes the liberty of calling the attention of Hon. W. Q. Gresham
                    to this obvious infringement of the neutrality laws, to the end that the
                    Government of the United States may be pleased to take, consistently with its
                    declarations, such measures as it may deem expedient.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">E. de Muruaga.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
